{"authored" [{"question" "q-108313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-1⟩+t⟨5,-2,4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩=22.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e91084ca6463f8dfa40c9cf75a3f2dee88d00a005a7e2d68df60aa979f6909c" "basis" 1917 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-108313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ 0(3+5t)+1(-2t)+(-2)(-1+4t) & =22 \\\\ -2t+2-8t & =22 \\\\ -10t & =20 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-2),-2(-2),-1+4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,4,-9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-7,4,-9).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e91084ca6463f8dfa40c9cf75a3f2dee88d00a005a7e2d68df60aa979f6909c" "basis" 1917 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-108313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dc