egin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ ⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ 5+3(-2+3t)+(-2)(3-t) & =-7 \\\\ 5-6+9t-6+2t & =-7 \\\\ 11t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5,-2+3(0),3-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,-2,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e91084ca6463f8dfa40c9cf75a3f2dee88d00a005a7e2d68df60aa979f6909c" "basis" 1917 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-108311" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a0a0f737738e6614dcf54d88095202b82a3ce826a18d4819f8dc807f491c853" "basis" 1917 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-108311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e91084ca6463f8dfa40c9cf75a3f2dee88d00a005a7e2d68df60aa979f6909c" "basis" 1917 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-108311" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(5,-2,3)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/ref